This code is a simple function that tells us how many milliseconds remain for free use after an expected 8 milliseconds of use for each frame rate in a VR mask
From our simple frame rate calculator, for 120 frames per second, our program has a total of about 0.3 milliseconds to run in order to avoid a bad experience given that 8 milliseconds are used by VR headset hardware.
- About 0.3 milliseconds computaional time for our program for a frame rate of 120Hz
- About 3.1 milliseconds computaional time for our program for a frame rate of 90Hz